{"text": "TO: Memorandum to the File\n\nFROM: Diana Grub Frieser\nCity Attorney\nDATE: November 22, 2011\n\nSUBJECT: Conflict of Interest Inquiry from Susan Haynie\n\nPart I: Basic Fact.\n\nOn Thursday, November 17, 2011, Susan Haynie contacted me regarding a potential conflict of interest.\nShe advised me of the following facts relating to the upcoming appeal of a site plan for 831 E. Palmetto\nPark Road (a property owned by James Batmasian, individually). She and her husband own a property\nmanagement company that manages numerous real property sites, but, in particular, has a property\nmanagement contract with a master condominium association for residential property in Broward County.\nThe master association is named Tivoli Park Master Association, Inc. (\u201cMaster Association\u201d) and is\ncomprised of three residential condominium associations. Ms. Haynie advised me that one of the three\ncondominium associations is a 200+ residential units complex that is owned wholly by the Batmasians\nand the units are made available for rental. The contract for property management services is an annual\ncontract and was entered into prior to the Palm Beach County ethics ordinance taking effect. The inquiry\nis whether the contractual relationship between Ms. Haynie\u2019s company and the Master Association\ncreates a voting conflict for Ms. Haynie in connection with the upcoming appeal to be heard by the City\nCouncil regarding 831 E. Palmetto Park Road.\n\nPart Il: Additional Information:\n\nWe obtained supplemental information from Ms. Haynie that demonstrates that the Master Association is\nactually comprised of six separate condominium associations or apartment complexes, with an aggregate\nof approximately 1600 units, and that all but approximately 200 of these units are owned or controlled\neither by the Batmasians and/or business entities in which they have a controlling interest. Additionally,\ntwo of the three listed officers of the Master Association are connected to Investments Ltd., which is a\nbusiness entity owned or controlled by the Batmasians.\n\nPart Ill: Analysis and Conclusion:\na. Florida Ethics Code of Ethics",
